  "theorem": "Among the three nonidentity native G60 deck involutions, exactly one induces on every signed Program-01 face the H65B connection-residual action: simultaneous swap within the positive registered pair and within the negative registered pair. The sealed Program-01 interface identifies that induced operator as S1=sigma_x K, which is anti-complex and fixes the neutral T axis. Using that same native involution as the diagonal G1800 kernel produces an exact two-state relative-lift torsor whose swap may be executed on either factor, [Bu,v]=[u,Bv]. Thus one upstairs joint relative-lift exchange has equivalent local Program-01 presentations as the selected anti-complex face reflection.",
